{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d3f6a2c4-8b1e-4a9f-9c2d-php-learning-api",
    "name": "PHP Learning English Web — API Regression",
    "description": "Regression / manual verification collection for the Laravel /api/v1 and /api/admin REST API (issue #28). This app authenticates via a Laravel session + CSRF cookie, NOT bearer tokens — matching admin-frontend/src/lib/api.ts's request() helper. A collection-level pre-request script fetches /api/v1/csrf-cookie and attaches X-XSRF-TOKEN to every mutating (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) request automatically, using Postman's cookie jar (requires Postman's cookie jar / 'Automatically follow redirects' defaults — no manual header copying needed).\n\nRun order (verified end-to-end with `newman run`):\n1. '0a - Login as Learner' before running '2 - Catalog' / '3 - Learning' / '4 - AI Proxy'.\n2. '0c - Logout' then '0b - Login as Admin' before running '5 - Admin Taxonomy' / '6 - Admin Users'.\n\nOnly one session is active in the shared cookie jar at a time. '0a'/'0b'/'0c' are deliberately separate top-level folders (not steps inside one folder) so that running any single one of them in a Collection Runner or `newman run --folder` does exactly what its name says, instead of silently chaining into logout.\n\nBefore running: `docker-compose exec app php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` to get known seed data (admin@example.com/admin123, user@example.com/user123, sample courses/lessons/quizzes, but NO Vocabulary rows — vocabulary only exists after a LexiLingo import/sync). '2 - Catalog' requests self-populate course_id/lesson_id into the environment via Tests scripts on first run; 'List Vocabulary' also tries to set vocabulary_id but will leave it empty on a fresh seed (see the note on '3 - Learning > Toggle Vocabulary Bookmark'). There is no public endpoint to list quiz ids, so quiz_id defaults to 1 (the first quiz created by LessonQuizSeeder on a fresh seed) — adjust manually if your seed data differs.\n\n'4 - AI Proxy' requests call the real configured LexiLingo AI service and will fail locally unless LEXILINGO_AI_URL/LEXILINGO_BACKEND_URL are set in the running app's .env — included for completeness, not guaranteed runnable out of the box.\n\n'8 - Learning Path, FSRS & Import Review' covers the self-owned Course Path, the non-mutating FSRS preview, Unit authoring and the staged import review flow. Log in as admin first ('0b'). 'Apply Import Run' is the only destructive request in the collection: it stays disabled unless FEATURE_LEXILINGO_IMPORT_APPLY=true, and a replacement additionally needs a fresh Google re-auth (428 otherwise), so 403/409/428/503 are expected passes there.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const mutating = ['POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE'];",
          "if (mutating.includes(pm.request.method)) {",
          "    pm.sendRequest({",
          "        url: pm.environment.get('base_url') + '/api/v1/csrf-cookie',",
          "        method: 'GET',",
          "        header: { Accept: 'application/json' }",
          "    }, function (err) {",
          "        if (err) { console.error('csrf-cookie fetch failed', err); return; }",
          "        pm.cookies.jar().get(pm.environment.get('base_url'), 'XSRF-TOKEN', function (err, token) {",
          "            if (!err && token) {",
          "                pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-XSRF-TOKEN', value: decodeURIComponent(token) });",
          "            }",
          "        });",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
